1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,175
A reference material, followed from the
bench to a laboratory that buys it,
through a recall, to an assessor asking
how you know.

2
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:20,000
This is Lotmark, a platform for producers
of certified reference materials. A
scientist signs in, and the console opens
on their own work.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,850
Two things are waiting: studies that need
his signature. Nothing here is a to-do
list somebody typed. It is the work
itself.

4
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:34,400
He opens the paracetamol project and finds
the study still in draft.

5
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:43,050
Signing it is not a click. The system asks
him to prove who he is, with his password
and a fresh authenticator code.

6
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:55,875
That is twenty one C F R part eleven: a
signature needs a fresh authentication,
not just a live session. Now the study is
signed, and it says who signed it and
when.

7
00:00:55,875 --> 00:01:00,850
The scientist has done their part. Now
somebody else takes over.

8
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:11,375
A second person authorises the certified
value. Whoever assigns a value never
authorises it — four eyes, enforced by the
server.

9
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:19,250
With an authorised value, a lot can be
released. It takes its own number and
supersedes the batch before it.

10
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:26,975
And the lot gets its certificate — the
document a laboratory will one day hold in
its hands and want to check.

11
00:01:26,975 --> 00:01:35,775
A laboratory buys that material. She signs
in to the same platform and sees an
entirely different world — her own.

12
00:01:35,775 --> 00:01:44,150
The catalogue carries only released lots
with an authorised value, each with its
certificate. She orders two units.

13
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:52,200
On the producer side, dispatch packs it
and sends it. A courier and a tracking
reference are attached as it goes.

14
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:59,225
This material ships between two and eight
degrees. The logger comes back with a
reading at fourteen.

15
00:01:59,225 --> 00:02:10,150
Nobody had to notice that. The excursion
raised a corrective action by itself,
because the readings are data rather than
a document somebody files.

16
00:02:10,150 --> 00:02:19,025
Quality moves it into investigation. Every
move is signed, states why, and joins a
history the card carries with it.

17
00:02:19,025 --> 00:02:27,350
And if the material itself is in doubt,
its certificate is withdrawn — and every
laboratory holding it is told.

18
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:33,525
Everything you have just watched is in the
ledger — every act, under the person who
did it.

19
00:02:33,525 --> 00:02:43,575
Each entry is hash-linked to the one
before it. Removing or altering one breaks
every link that follows, and the console
will say so.

20
00:02:43,575 --> 00:02:53,425
Even the configuration changes under
signature. A draft is reviewed, signed,
and becomes a numbered version records are
pinned to.

21
00:02:53,425 --> 00:03:03,100
And the certificate can be checked by
anyone holding it. No account, no login —
an assessor with a printed certificate
should not need one.
